// `dragon-death`'s steps (D620): the bot, an operator, in survival mode with resistance IV and
// 1000 health 20 east of the end fixture's spawn, where mob griefing's off, takes an axe sharp
// enough to kill and summons over it an ender dragon with AI and 1 health landing, which flies
// toward the egg's place; the bot hits it on its way, so it's dying with its health left at 1,
// flying on toward the top of the podium, and once it's within 10 of it, its health 0, it dies,
// rising for 200 ticks, its experience given, and it's gone.
fn dragon_death_steps() -> List<(str, str)> {
    return [
        ("item replace entity @s weapon.mainhand with minecraft:netherite_axe[enchantments=\{sharpness:255\}]", "dragon-death-axe"),
        ("summon ender_dragon ~ ~4 ~ \{DragonPhase:3,Health:1f\}", "dragon-death-summoned"),
