// `wolf-shake`'s steps (CAL-201), where `snow-golems`' are: by day, the bot, in creative mode,
// summons a wolf and sets water in its block, which wets it and flows about it; then takes the
// water away, sets it again a second later and takes it away again. As the flow spreads and
// drains about it, the wolf, wet, on the ground and finding no path, starts to shake itself dry,
// `Wolf.aiStep`, entity event 8, and stops each time it's back in water, entity event 56, till
// out of it at last it shakes for 2 seconds, heard. It watches for 4 seconds after.
fn wolf_shake_steps() -> List<(str, str)> {
    return [
        ("time set day", "wolf-shake-day"),
        ("gamemode creative", "wolf-shake-creative"),
        ("summon wolf -8.5 -60 0.5", "wolf-shake-wolf"),
        ("setblock -9 -60 0 water", "wolf-shake-water"),
        ("", "wolf-shake-wet-1"), ("", "wolf-shake-wet-2"),
        ("setblock -9 -60 0 air", "wolf-shake-dry"),
        ("", "wolf-shake-shaking"),
        ("setblock -9 -60 0 water", "wolf-shake-water-again"),
        ("", "wolf-shake-stopped-1"), ("", "wolf-shake-stopped-2"),
        ("setblock -9 -60 0 air", "wolf-shake-dry-again"),
        ("", "wolf-shake-5"), ("", "wolf-shake-6"), ("", "wolf-shake-7"), ("", "wolf-shake-8"),
        ("", "wolf-shake-after"),
    ]
}

// `wolf-tame`'s steps (CAL-201), where `wolves`' are: by day, the bot, in survival mode, walls a
// pen west of it in glass two high and summons a wolf in it, and holds twelve bones, using them on
// it one by one; each is one in three to tame it, drawn, entity event 7, else event 6,
// `Wolf.mobInteract`, tamed one ordered to sit, the ones after ordering it to stand or sit, the
// owner's use that does nothing else. It dyes its collar
// blue, hits it, which stands it, `Wolf.hurtServer`, and feeds it beef, which heals it, then goes
// 14 blocks east, where it follows, `FollowOwnerGoal`, or, 12 or more off, teleports to it. It
// watches for 4 seconds.
